[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: A client without a daemon fails loudly and does nothing else

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-SCRIBE-CLIENT-FAILS-CLOSED
TITLE: A client without a daemon fails loudly and does nothing else
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
A scribe client shall treat an unreachable daemon as an error. It shall not
load the graph in its own process, shall not start a daemon, and shall not
answer from a cache.

It shall name the socket it looked for and the command that starts a daemon,
and exit non-zero.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-SCRIBE-DAEMON-NO-FALLBACK
  ROLE: Governed_By
